<title>USA: Consumers Mich. nuke shuts for repairs.</title>
<headline>Consumers Mich. nuke shuts for repairs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Energy's 67 megawatt Big Rock Point nuclear power unit was shut Sunday to repair a leak, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Charlevoix, Mich., is expected to return to service on March 13, the NRC report stated.</p>
<p>Consumers is a unit of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
